{"id":210461960545621,"type":"genre","name":"El soul conquista Gran Bretaña","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":24,"info":{"img":null},"own_scenes":[{"id":65,"name":"El soul conquista Gran Bretaña","book":{"id":1,"slug":"1966_Savage","title":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/","families":{"beat":{"name":"Beat británico, mod y freakbeat","color":"#ef4444"},"garage":{"name":"Garage y punk americano","color":"#f97316"},"folk":{"name":"Folk rock y canción protesta","color":"#a3e635"},"psico":{"name":"Psicodelia, LSD y raga rock","color":"#c084fc"},"pop":{"name":"Pop de estudio: Spector, Beach Boys, Meek","color":"#38bdf8"},"soul":{"name":"Soul, Motown, R&B y ska","color":"#facc15"},"vanguardia":{"name":"Vanguardia: Warhol, Velvet, free jazz, arte","color":"#e5e7eb"},"juventud":{"name":"Juventud, moda y medios: Swinging London, radio pirata","color":"#f472b6"},"politica":{"name":"Política: CND, Vietnam, derechos civiles, feminismo, gays","color":"#22d3ee"}}},"family":"Soul, Motown, R&B y ska","color":"#facc15","start":1961,"end":1967,"place":"Londres (Soho, Tiles), Mánchester (Twisted Wheel)","desc":"El 26 de octubre «Reach Out I’ll Be There» de los Four Tops, con la flauta de aire oriental, el fraseo dylaniano de Lamont Dozier y la interpretación de su vida de Levi Stubbs, desbancó a «Distant Drums» y fue número 1: el momento en que la música negra americana ocupó el centro de la cultura juvenil británica, al revés que en el boom del beat. Lo habían preparado durante años los entusiastas: Dave Godin, que fundó en 1963 la Tamla Motown Appreciation Society, viajó a Detroit, llevó «Where Did Our Love Go» a los piratas y bautizó el sello Tamla Motown (marzo de 1965, con una gira de la revista que fracasó fuera de Londres); Guy Stevens, que pinchaba discos negros en el Scene y dirigió Sue Records para Chris Blackwell; Roger Eagle en el Twisted Wheel de Mánchester; Tony Hall promocionando Atlantic («In the Midnight Hour», el «My Girl» de Otis Redding); el DJ Jeff Dexter mezclando soul y ska en Tiles, el club subterráneo de Oxford Street del mod de masas que visitó Tom Wolfe. En otoño de 1966 Atlantic y Motown copaban las listas; Otis Redding metió a 8.000 personas en Tiles; los Four Tops arrasaron en el Savile de Brian Epstein el 13 de noviembre. El racismo, aun así, seguía ahí.","aka":["Tamla Motown","the Scene","Twisted Wheel","Sue Records","rock’n’soul","Tiles"],"notes":[],"influences":[{"name":"Motown: Supremes y Holland-Dozier-Holland","id":259223984112705,"type":"genre"},{"name":"Soul sureño: Stax, Atlantic y FAME","id":205122640489566,"type":"genre"},{"name":"Mods","id":129048513133743,"type":"genre"},{"name":"Radio pirata","id":178594019675310,"type":"genre"}],"refs":[{"ch":12,"q":"On 1 November, Britain had a new #1.","para":"On 1 November, Britain had a new #1. The morbid miasma of ‘Distant Drums’ had finally been dispelled, on 26 October, by a record so strong and so unexpected that it hit the country with all the force of a hurricane. The Four Tops’ ‘Reach Out I’ll Be There’ had received unprecedented pre-release raves earlier in the month: it was ‘a knockout disc’, ‘the most important record of the year’. Penny Valentine went even further: ‘If you have ever been lonely, if you have any soul or any heart at all, you must go and buy this disc now.’","page":486,"pdf":318,"chapter":"Noviembre: Good Vibrations: Motown y el soul en Reino Unido, los Beach Boys y el Sunset Strip"},{"ch":12,"q":"The record begins with a flute fanfare, part ominous, part Near Eastern","para":"The record begins with a flute fanfare, part ominous, part Near Eastern; a clicking rhythm guitar and rumbling bass set up a fast, syncopated rhythm. Levi Stubbs enters, near the top of his range, singing lyrics that gave the year’s dark preoccupations an entirely different spin: ‘And your life is filled with much confusion / Until happiness is just an illusion.’ Underscored by the Tops’ wordless exclamation under the first line, the song has an incredible forward drive, so much so that it dispenses with a middle eight in the headlong quest for resolution.","page":487,"pdf":318,"chapter":"Noviembre: Good Vibrations: Motown y el soul en Reino Unido, los Beach Boys y el Sunset Strip"},{"ch":12,"q":"It had been a long time coming.","para":"It had been a long time coming. The British taste for black American music had been established from the early years of the twentieth century on, with the successive popularity of the cakewalk, ragtime, blues and jazz. But access to the real thing was limited, thanks to the difficulty and expense of transatlantic travel, the practice of white artists covering black R&B and rock ’n’ roll hits, and the lack of any radio exposure outside the BBC. Even in the 1950s, black American music enthusiasts like Dave Godin found themselves ‘like orphans in a storm’.","page":492,"pdf":321,"chapter":"Noviembre: Good Vibrations: Motown y el soul en Reino Unido, los Beach Boys y el Sunset Strip"},{"ch":12,"q":"Formed in 1963, the Tamla Motown Appreciation Society helped to fuel the growing groundswell of black American music in the UK.","para":"Formed in 1963, the Tamla Motown Appreciation Society helped to fuel the growing groundswell of black American music in the UK. Apart from Norman Jopling’s regular bulletins in Record Mirror, there was a fresh push by British record companies to release American material. EMI’s Stateside label issued singles by the Isley Brothers, the Shirelles, the Jaynetts and, from October 1963 – beginning with Martha and the Vandellas’ ‘Heat Wave’ – material from Berry Gordy’s various labels.","page":493,"pdf":322,"chapter":"Noviembre: Good Vibrations: Motown y el soul en Reino Unido, los Beach Boys y el Sunset Strip"},{"ch":12,"q":"By autumn, the wave of black American music had become unstoppable.","para":"By autumn, the wave of black American music had become unstoppable. Dammed up for so long, it flooded a British pop scene floundering in the wake of Swinging London. In September, Billboard recorded the fact that Atlantic Records, flourishing under its new UK deal with Polydor, was ‘the hottest American label in England right now, with five records dominating the English market’.","page":507,"pdf":329,"chapter":"Noviembre: Good Vibrations: Motown y el soul en Reino Unido, los Beach Boys y el Sunset Strip"}],"artists":[{"id":181531864823591,"type":"artist","name":"The Supremes","rating":null},{"id":191426406604859,"type":"artist","name":"The Temptations","rating":null},{"id":103562045205386,"type":"artist","name":"The Drifters","rating":null},{"id":206553628925579,"type":"artist","name":"The Everly Brothers","rating":null},{"id":252678611065802,"type":"artist","name":"The Four Tops","rating":null},{"id":94962106944085,"type":"artist","name":"The Marvelettes","rating":null},{"id":105187608930066,"type":"artist","name":"Otis Redding","rating":null},{"id":97139443064313,"type":"artist","name":"Billy Preston","rating":null},{"id":145727222532186,"type":"artist","name":"The Ronettes","rating":null},{"id":45543175710038,"type":"artist","name":"Prince Buster","rating":null},{"id":126399970369228,"type":"artist","name":"Chris Blackwell","rating":null},{"id":209290337278435,"type":"artist","name":"Millie Small","rating":null},{"id":26407202654392,"type":"artist","name":"Lamont Dozier","rating":null},{"id":152073179001591,"type":"artist","name":"Ike & Tina Turner","rating":null},{"id":103627988357339,"type":"artist","name":"The Wailers","rating":null},{"id":78676651227411,"type":"artist","name":"Dion","rating":null},{"id":103552482129650,"type":"artist","name":"Lee Dorsey","rating":null},{"id":224728012070362,"type":"artist","name":"Wilbert Harrison","rating":null},{"id":76370969490465,"type":"artist","name":"Alvin Cash and the Registers","rating":null},{"id":271684055107895,"type":"artist","name":"Eddie Floyd","rating":null},{"id":13680935320435,"type":"artist","name":"Dobie Gray","